                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I’ve played a LOT of horror RPG Maker games over the years, and honestly, Red Haze is probably my favorite one.\n\nThere’s just something about the atmosphere in this game that really got to me. It’s eerie without having to constantly throw jumpscares at you, and the voice acting and soundtrack are both amazing. They add a lot to the whole experience.\n\nIf you’re into horror RPG Maker games, I definitely recommend giving this one a try. I think it’s still listed as Early Access, but honestly, it feels pretty much finished at this point. You can already access most of the game, so I wouldn’t let the Early Access label put you off.\n\nI’ve played most of Yai Gameworks’ games and they always seem to have something unique about them. They don’t just feel like the same game with a different story. There’s always some little thing that makes each one stand out.\n\nRed Haze definitely didn’t disappoint me. I really love what they’re doing with these games.\n\nThis is art.",
